WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.377
[g@The Daoist had vanished!

2
00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:09.898
Wukong ran outside and shot into the air.@g]

3
00:00:09.899 --> 00:00:12.606
He looked in every direction.

4
00:00:12.607 --> 00:00:15.689
"Where did the Daoist go?" asked the monkey.

5
00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:19.267
Then he heard a shout from inside the palace.

6
00:00:19.268 --> 00:00:26.386
"There are two Tang Monks!" cried Bajie.

7
00:00:26.387 --> 00:00:31.505
[g@Wukong flew back inside.

8
00:00:31.506 --> 00:00:35.384
Two Tang Monks stood side by side.@g]

9
00:00:35.385 --> 00:00:38.381
[g@"We can't tell them apart," said Wujing.

10
00:00:38.382 --> 00:00:40.765
"They look exactly alike."@g]

11
00:00:40.766 --> 00:00:45.253
"Which one of you is the real Tang Monk?" asked Wukong.

12
00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:47.212
"I am!" said one.

13
00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:51.508
The other monk glared at the first one. "No, I am!"

14
00:00:51.509 --> 00:00:54.016
The first monk looked at Wukong.

15
00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:55.806
[g@"Don't believe him, Wukong.

16
00:00:55.807 --> 00:00:58.209
I am the real Tang Monk."@g]

17
00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.936
[g@"Don't believe [i@him!@i]" said the other monk.

18
00:01:00.937 --> 00:01:04.255
"[i@I@i] am the real Tang Monk."@g]

19
00:01:04.256 --> 00:01:08.822
Angry, Wukong pulled out his iron bar.

20
00:01:08.823 --> 00:01:12.371
"Which one of you is the real Tang Monk?"

21
00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:16.610
Both Tang Monks fell to their knees, shaking with fear.

22
00:01:16.611 --> 00:01:20.636
"Don't hit me!" they both cried.

23
00:01:20.637 --> 00:01:22.465
[g@The monkey sighed.

24
00:01:22.466 --> 00:01:24.812
He turned to Bajie and Wujing.

25
00:01:24.813 --> 00:01:28.649
"What can we do?"@g]

26
00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:32.141
[g@"I have an idea," said Bajie, smiling.

27
00:01:32.142 --> 00:01:34.382
"But you won't like it."@g]

28
00:01:34.383 --> 00:01:39.146
"What is it?" asked Wukong.

29
00:01:39.147 --> 00:01:43.834
"The two Tang Monks should recite the Tight Headband spell," said the pig.

30
00:01:43.835 --> 00:01:49.176
"Only the Tang Monk, Guanyin, and Buddha know the spell.

31
00:01:49.177 --> 00:01:52.919
We'll know right away which Tang Monk is fake."

32
00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.502
"You just want to see me in pain!" said Wukong.

33
00:01:57.503 --> 00:02:02.932
Then he sighed. "But it is a good idea."

34
00:02:02.933 --> 00:02:07.319
Bajie and Wujing stood near the monks.

35
00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.958
"Master, recite the Tight Headband spell," said Wukong.

36
00:02:11.959 --> 00:02:16.989
Both monks began speaking, and Wukong fell to the floor.

37
00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:20.130
"It hurts!" he cried.

38
00:02:20.131 --> 00:02:23.645
Bajie watched the Tang Monks carefully.

39
00:02:23.646 --> 00:02:26.794
[g@One of them was reciting the spell.

40
00:02:26.795 --> 00:02:29.318
But the other one wasn't.@g]

41
00:02:29.319 --> 00:02:33.217
"This is the fake Tang Monk!" shouted the pig, pointing.

42
00:02:33.218 --> 00:02:36.643
"He's just mumbling nonsense!"

43
00:02:36.644 --> 00:02:40.163
The real monk stopped reciting the spell.

44
00:02:40.164 --> 00:02:43.960
Bajie and Wujing tried to grab the fake monk.

45
00:02:43.961 --> 00:02:50.422
But the monk changed into a green lion and ran out of the throne room.

46
00:02:50.423 --> 00:02:53.222
"Get him!" shouted Wukong.

47
00:02:53.223 --> 00:02:56.827
He and his companions chased the lion.

48
00:02:56.828 --> 00:03:00.655
Outside, the lion leaped into the air.

49
00:03:00.656 --> 00:03:03.490
Wukong and the others shot after him.

50
00:03:03.491 --> 00:03:08.958
Clouds swirled, and soon they had the lion surrounded.

51
00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:13.852
Wukong pulled out his iron bar and raised it to strike.

52
00:03:13.853 --> 00:03:19.827
Just then a deep voice called out, "Do not hit him, Sun Wukong!"

53
00:03:19.828 --> 00:03:22.824
Everyone looked up.

54
00:03:22.825 --> 00:03:26.615
"It's the bodhisattva Manjusri!" said Wukong.

55
00:03:26.616 --> 00:03:30.459
"This green lion is my pet," said the bodhisattva.

56
00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:35.723
"The king of the Black Rooster Kingdom was cruel to someone many years ago.

57
00:03:35.724 --> 00:03:39.049
[g@So my lion came to Earth to punish him.

58
00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:42.804
The king's punishment is over now."@g]

59
00:03:42.805 --> 00:03:47.881
The bodhisattva and the lion disappeared above the clouds.

60
00:03:47.882 --> 00:03:52.600
That night the king of the Black Rooster Kingdom hosted a feast.

61
00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:56.568
[g@During the feast he turned to the Tang Monk.

62
00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.764
"Thank you for your help.@g]

63
00:03:58.765 --> 00:04:04.671
I hope you will reach the Western Paradise very soon."

64
00:04:04.672 --> 00:04:09.755
Weeks passed, and the travelers continued west.

65
00:04:09.756 --> 00:04:15.450
One day Wukong saw a mysterious red cloud over the mountains ahead.

66
00:04:15.451 --> 00:04:19.173
"Stop walking," he said quietly.

67
00:04:19.174 --> 00:04:22.634
"What's wrong?" asked the Tang Monk.

68
00:04:22.635 --> 00:04:24.653
[g@The red cloud disappeared.

69
00:04:24.654 --> 00:04:27.627
Wukong shook his head.@g]

70
00:04:27.628 --> 00:04:32.287
"Nothing, Master. I thought I saw a red cloud."

71
00:04:32.288 --> 00:04:35.411
[g@They walked some more.

72
00:04:35.412 --> 00:04:38.506
Wukong saw the red cloud again.@g]

73
00:04:38.507 --> 00:04:41.813
He held up his hand for the others to stop.

74
00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:47.276
The red cloud disappeared once again, and Wukong started to walk again.

75
00:04:47.277 --> 00:04:50.552
But then the red cloud reappeared.

76
00:04:50.553 --> 00:04:52.656
"Stop," said the monkey.

77
00:04:52.657 --> 00:04:54.786
[g@The Tang Monk groaned.

78
00:04:54.787 --> 00:05:02.583
"Wukong, should we keep going or not?"@g]

